      "value": "<ac:layout><ac:layout-section ac:type=\"two_right_sidebar\" ac:breakout-mode=\"default\"><ac:layout-cell><p>This page describes Odoo inventory relevant setup and configuration, following which you can effectively manage inventory integrated with Bahmni Clinical features.&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</p><h1>Warehouse &amp; Locations</h1><p>In Odoo 16, Storage Location tracking needs to be enabled. The same can be enabled or disabled from <code>Menu -&gt; Settings -&gt; Inventory -&gt; Warehouse</code>. In the screen enable the Storage Locations toggle to track stock by locations.</p><ac:image ac:align=\"center\" ac:layout=\"center\" ac:original-height=\"682\" ac:original-width=\"1792\" ac:custom-width=\"true\" ac:alt=\"image-20240812-155927.png\" ac:width=\"871\"><ri:attachment ri:filename=\"image-20240812-155927.png\" ri:version-at-save=\"1\" /></ac:image><p /><ac:structured-macro ac:name=\"expand\" ac:schema-version=\"1\" ac:macro-id=\"a2a0aacb-6fc0-4972-8ee8-bfe04f5f6fec\"><ac:parameter ac:name=\"title\">Odoo 10 Warehouse and Location Configuration</ac:parameter><ac:rich-text-body><p>Go to &quot;Menu / Inventory / Configuration / Settings&quot;, and find setting for &ldquo;Location &amp; Warehouse&rdquo;. Check for configuration element <strong>&quot;Warehouses and Locations usage level&quot;</strong> and choose your option.</p><ol start=\"1\"><li><p>Manage only 1 Warehouse with only 1 stock location - this is the simplest of setup</p></li><li><p>Manage only 1 Warehouse, composed by several stock locations - our examples in WIKI, assumes such a setup.&nbsp;</p></li><li><p>Manage several Warehouses, each one composed by several stock locations -&nbsp;for advanced and more complicated setup. </p></li></ol><p>If you have chosen multiple warehouse/locations, you should see it reflect under your &ldquo;Inventory&rdquo; landing page.&nbsp;</p></ac:rich-text-body></ac:structured-macro><p /><p>You can define different &ldquo;Internal&rdquo;&nbsp;inventory locations like &quot;Main Stock Room&quot;, &ldquo;OPD Pharmacy&rdquo;, &ldquo;IPD Pharmacy&rdquo;, &ldquo;Procedure Room&rdquo;, &quot;Samples Stock&quot; under the a warehouse<strong>. </strong>So the hierarchy may be</p><ul><li><p>WH (Warehouse Name)</p><ul><li><p>WH/Stock = the main stock room (this would be created by default, usually).&nbsp;</p></li><li><p>WH/OPD&nbsp;Pharmacy&nbsp; &nbsp;= OPD Pharmacy stock room</p></li><li><p>WH/IPD&nbsp;Pharmacy&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;= IPD Pharmacy stock room</p></li><li><p>WH/Procedure Room = Surgery Stock Room</p></li><li><p>WH/Samples Stock&nbsp; &nbsp; = Maybe Doctor's received samples stock room where doctors may give away meds at his/her discretion.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p></li></ul></li></ul><p>You can setup Warehouses and Locations by accessing configuration of Inventory module at <code>Menu -&gt; Inventory -&gt; Configuration</code></p><ac:image ac:align=\"center\" ac:layout=\"center\" ac:original-height=\"351\" ac:original-width=\"1792\" ac:custom-width=\"true\" ac:alt=\"image-20240812-160048.png\" ac:width=\"871\"><ri:attachment ri:filename=\"image-20240812-160048.png\" ri:version-at-save=\"1\" /></ac:image><p /><h1>Product Relevant Configuration</h1><p><span style=\"color: rgb(76,76,76);\">Go to &quot;Menu / Inventory / Configuration / Settings&quot;. The most relevant configurations are described below, but you should review other configuration elements that might apply for your implementation</span></p><h2><span style=\"color: rgb(76,76,76);\">Traceability Settings</span></h2><ul><li><p>Enable&nbsp;<strong>&ldquo;Track lots or serial numbers&rdquo;. </strong>This will enable product tracking by lot or serial number, which is relevant for medications or other consumables. Note: You may still decide to have &ldquo;no tracking&rdquo; (by lots/serial number) at individual product level.&nbsp;</p></li><li><p>Enable <strong>&ldquo;Expiration Dates&rdquo; </strong>to specify expiration for each serial numbers</p></li></ul><ac:image ac:align=\"center\" ac:layout=\"center\" ac:original-height=\"276\" ac:original-width=\"1792\" ac:custom-width=\"true\" ac:alt=\"image-20240812-160149.png\" ac:width=\"847\"><ri:attachment ri:filename=\"image-20240812-160149.png\" ri:version-at-save=\"1\" /></ac:image><p /><h2>Products&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(76,76,76);\">Settings</span></h2><ul><li><p><strong>&ldquo;Units of Measure&rdquo; :</strong>&nbsp;Choose &ldquo;Some products may be sold/purchased in different units of measure (advanced)&rdquo;.&nbsp; </p><ul><li><p>You should be able to see some predefined &ldquo;Units of Measure&rdquo; already present under &quot;Configuration / Units of measure&quot; menu.&nbsp;</p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong>&quot;Product Variants&quot;: </strong>choose option &quot;No variants&quot; or &quot;<span style=\"color: rgb(76,76,76);\">Products can have several attributes, defining variants&quot; as applicable.</span></p></li></ul><h2>Product Categories</h2><p>Go to &quot;Menu / Inventory / Configuration / Products / Product Categories&quot;.</p><ul><li><p>You should see some predefined category hierarchy. for example: you may want to create a category called &ldquo;Fees and Charges&rdquo; under &ldquo;All / Services&rdquo; for any type of Service that you may define, like Specialist Fee, Minor Dressing Fee etc.&nbsp;</p></li><li><p>You may also want to re-organize the product categories in hierarchies. Typically, the product categories are hierarchized as &quot;All / Saleable&quot; and &quot;All / Services&quot;. Your category hierarchy may look like below&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ac:image ac:align=\"center\" ac:layout=\"center\" ac:original-height=\"885\" ac:original-width=\"587\" ac:custom-width=\"true\" ac:alt=\"image-20240812-160437.png\" ac:width=\"587\"><ri:attachment ri:filename=\"image-20240812-160437.png\" ri:version-at-save=\"1\" /></ac:image><h2>Individual Product Specification</h2><p>Once the products are synchronized from OpenMRS, you may want to configure each products.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>Go to &ldquo;Menu / Inventory / Products&rdquo; and search for a product and edit. e.g &ldquo;Ibuprofen 400mg&rdquo;</p><ul><li><p>Usually, Drugs etc will be synced as product type &ldquo;Saleable Product&rdquo; that can be stocked, and Lab tests/Radiology tests etc will be synced as &ldquo;Service&rdquo;.&nbsp;</p></li><li><p>In &ldquo;General information&rdquo; tab, configure properties like &ldquo;Sales Price&rdquo;, &ldquo;Cost Price&rdquo;, &ldquo;MRP&rdquo;, &ldquo;Units of Measure&rdquo; etc</p></li><li><p>In &ldquo;Inventory&rdquo; tab, configure properties like Routes (Buy or Make to order), tracking options (No tracking, by serial number, by lots&rdquo;, vendors for this product etc (especially for stockable product)</p></li></ul><p>NOTE: Tracking options are important, especially if you are managing purchases through Odoo and dispensing drugs by lots or serial number.&nbsp;</p><ac:image ac:align=\"center\" ac:layout=\"center\" ac:original-height=\"762\" ac:original-width=\"1126\" ac:custom-width=\"true\" ac:width=\"871\"><ri:attachment ri:filename=\"Screenshot 2024-08-12 at 9.35.23 PM.png\" ri:version-at-save=\"1\" /></ac:image><p /><h1>Customize Product Lots/Serial list view (only for Odoo 10)</h1><ac:adf-extension><ac:adf-node type=\"panel\"><ac:adf-attribute key=\"panel-type\">note</ac:adf-attribute><ac:adf-content><p>This is needed only in Odoo 10. Odoo 16 comes preconfigured with this extension fields displayed.</p></ac:adf-content></ac:adf-node><ac:adf-fallback><div class=\"panel conf-macro output-block\" style=\"background-color: rgb(234,230,255);border-color: rgb(153,141,217);border-width: 1.0px;\"><div class=\"panelContent\" style=\"background-color: rgb(234,230,255);\">\n<p>This is needed only in Odoo 10. Odoo 16 comes preconfigured with this extension fields displayed.</p>\n</div></div></ac:adf-fallback></ac:adf-extension><p>If you have enabled product tracking by &ldquo;lots/serial number&rdquo;, and you follow a purchase/receive process for that product, you can define sale price for each lot while receiving the products.&nbsp;</p><p>List of lots/serial information can be viewed form &ldquo;Menu / Inventory / Inventory Control / Lots/Serial Number&rdquo;. By default the screen shows up with a table showing fields - &ldquo;lot/serial number&rdquo;, &ldquo;reference&rdquo;, &ldquo;product&rdquo;.&nbsp;</p><ac:image ac:align=\"center\" ac:layout=\"wide\" ac:original-height=\"452\" ac:original-width=\"2324\" ac:width=\"680\"><ri:attachment ri:filename=\"Odoo_default_Lots_Serial_View.png\" ri:version-at-save=\"1\" /></ac:image><p /><p>If you would like to see fields like &ldquo;cost price&rdquo;, &ldquo;sale price&rdquo; and &ldquo;expiry date&rdquo;, you need to customize the odoo default view. To do this see follow instructions below</p><ol start=\"1\"><li><p>Enable developer mode</p></li><li><p>Go to&ldquo;Menu / Inventory / Inventory Control / Lots/Serial Number&rdquo;, and from Odoo developer tools (top right corner), select &ldquo;edit treeview&rdquo;, edit the XML view definition and add the following fields.&nbsp;</p><p /><p><strong>Losts TreeView</strong></p><ac:structured-macro ac:name=\"code\" ac:schema-version=\"1\" ac:macro-id=\"ce140b1b-298b-40a7-be16-06bd5b9c4e05\"><ac:parameter ac:name=\"language\">text</ac:parameter><ac:plain-text-body><![CDATA[    ....\n    <field name=\"cost_price\"/>\n    <field name=\"sale_price\"/>\n    <field name=\"life_date\"/>]]></ac:plain-text-body></ac:structured-macro><p /></li><li><p>Save and reload the page. You should see the view like below with additional columns</p><ac:image ac:align=\"center\" ac:layout=\"center\" ac:original-height=\"466\" ac:original-width=\"2346\"><ri:attachment ri:filename=\"Odoo_customized_Lots_Serial_View.png\" ri:version-at-save=\"1\" /></ac:image></li></ol></ac:layout-cell><ac:layout-cell><p /><ac:structured-macro ac:name=\"tip\" ac:schema-version=\"1\" ac:macro-id=\"9550b5b8-4445-4cfa-91cc-fcc181bc5543\"><ac:rich-text-body><h3>On this Page</h3></ac:rich-text-body></ac:structured-macro><ac:structured-macro ac:name=\"toc\" ac:schema-version=\"1\" data-layout=\"default\" ac:local-id=\"36a14b24-f633-4515-b391-b68b3496853e\" ac:macro-id=\"704a085e-9e1b-4ca9-8d30-19a041972b88\"><ac:parameter ac:name=\"maxLevel\">6</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name=\"minLevel\">1</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name=\"include\" /><ac:parameter ac:name=\"outline\">false</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name=\"indent\" /><ac:parameter ac:name=\"exclude\" /><ac:parameter ac:name=\"style\">default</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name=\"type\">list</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name=\"printable\">true</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name=\"class\" /></ac:structured-macro><p /><ac:structured-macro ac:name=\"panel\" ac:schema-version=\"1\" data-layout=\"default\" ac:local-id=\"d2189dde-1689-463c-b589-3d27460f5d37\" ac:macro-id=\"93152c5d-6bea-40d9-a973-a55a64c04d31\"><ac:parameter ac:name=\"titleColor\">white</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name=\"titleBGColor\">#1FA5A0</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name=\"title\">Related Links</ac:parameter><ac:rich-text-body><p><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9KPeGFyWa18\">Odoo Inventory, Warehouse Management</a> (Odoo webinar)</p><p><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Zj8_8Uh3EAo\">Inventory 10 Management, Products</a> (Odoo webinar)</p><p><a href=\"https://www.odoo.com/documentation/16.0/applications/inventory_and_mrp/inventory.html\">Odoo 16 Inventory Management</a> (Official Docs)</p></ac:rich-text-body></ac:structured-macro><p /></ac:layout-cell></ac:layout-section></ac:layout>",
